# Six word-sized identifiers with no name

`r53` `r5d` `r5e` `r5f` `r63` `r6a` -- each has a slot of its own in the firmware, so the variable is real. But all six read zero in the single scan there is: something has to move them.

## How to capture

An ordinary ride, but with the extremes:

- long closed-throttle runs down from 4000+ -- engine braking;
- full throttle to the limiter at least once;
- a warm-up to the fan and a stand in traffic;
- a hot restart after ten minutes stopped.

## What to watch for

Any of the six leaving zero for even one sample is the condition, found. Write down what it was, and repeat it to tell a channel from a glitch.
